{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103383-2e-paternostern-ministry-members","id":1103383,"title":"[2E] Paternostern Ministry members","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T21:41:21-07:00","id":1103383,"title":"[2E] Paternostern Ministry members","content":"I must say, I have a greatest problem with Paternostern Ministry as written. Oddly, my Hieromagus, globetrotting chronicle would use this as those are written in books. But I need serving pylon for one of Ministry Secretaries ( Cardinal of Christanity ) or Librarian of Ministry. Best as pylon would be on Archeomancy bent - but Paternostern generally is, from what I know. I just have problem of envisioning 'evil Christianity priest' mages past Cardinal in Rome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bonus points for putting somehow high Spirit or Matter Arcana in this group.<br /> <br /> Also, do not Paternostern have they own 'strong arm', own fighters, so they do not need Pretorians to do their combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T22:20:51-07:00","id":1103388,"title":"","content":"I'm trusting you know they're not just 'Christian.' They have their own 'true' religion, of which the Patriarch is the top god. If you're familiar with GI Joe, at least IDW's more modern run, Serpentor is a good example of a member of the Ministry, heading up a Scientology-like cult among the rich and famous while preaching the true faith to his fellows in Cobra. I'm sure there's more obvious and popular examples, misleading and outright sinister religious types are all over.<br /> <br /> The Paternoster doesn't have Librarians. Instead they have Evangelines who destroy or bury 'truly inspired art,' that might hint at the Supernal. The Pentacle fears that they also start banal and spiritually debilitating art trends.<br /> <br /> As for warriors they have templars from the Order of the Temple of Sophia. They also have Hollow Ones, who are sort of people with damaged souls who Mind magic works easier on, automatically granting the Advanced Duration in first edition. The Ministry also has consciousness gems that have stock personalities they can then use on the Hollow ones to imprint personalities upon.<br /> <br /> Someone with a focus on Spirit magic would be able to use their spirits as catspaws in their attempts to mislead mortals. It would be an easy way to keep tabs on and influence minor and major religious centers in their territory, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-14-2017, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T23:09:15-07:00","id":1103394,"title":"","content":"While it's pretty textbook, Frollo from the Hunchback of Notre Dame is excellent for the Paternoster.<br /> The song Hellfire is especially good for seeing how the interaction between your Prelacy and your own desires might not always leave you happy.<br /> <br /> But more generally?<br /> Anyone who makes others blind slaves to dogma could be Paternoster material.<br /> I've been tossing up the thought of mass-media communication of scientific information to the masses as a tool of the Paternoster.<br /> Primarily because so many people believe whatever they hear about scientific advancements as being true just because it was reported.<br /> How it mentions they seek to bind people blindly to atheism the same as other 'false' religions is quite interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T23:55:31-07:00","id":1103399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103383-2e-paternostern-ministry-members?p=1103388#post1103388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trusting you know they're not just 'Christian.' They have their own 'true' religion, of which the Patriarch is the top god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know that whole Ministry is MUCH larger than Churches of Christ, with all other religions - Judaism, Islam, Buddism, Shinto, etc. - being part of it. But this particular pylon - working under Cardinal of Christanity - will ofcoruse come from original Christian lot. To ease the group they will answer to real Catholic cardinal in Sleepers Church - <i>Pontifex Maximus</i> - but will have connections in Church of England ( from Knights of Saint George contacts ).<br /> <br /> Defending world from future coming of ( false, in their view ) Messiaha of Magic seems appropriate to ex-Christian Paternostern members, for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1103383-2e-paternostern-ministry-members?p=1103394#post1103394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's pretty textbook, Frollo from the Hunchback of Notre Dame is excellent for the Paternoster.<br /> The song Hellfire is especially good for seeing how the interaction between your Prelacy and your own desires might not always leave you happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will rewatch today <b>Hunchback</b> then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-14-2017, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T00:19:25-07:00","id":1103404,"title":"","content":"The Catholic Church has archivists and priests in it you know. They also have a vested interest in protecting and maintaining a huge number of holy sites from churches to historical locations. An archaeomancer bent isn't even a stretch of the imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T01:23:08-07:00","id":1103414,"title":"","content":"Question is more if all proper Paternoster Ministry members should be priests or pastors? In Middle Ages monks and copyists are obvious candidates, but in modern Churches those positions are almost unheard off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}